{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1190607-hunter-s-question-difference-between-bystander-s-and-innocent-s","id":1190607,"title":"Hunter's Question Difference between bystander's and Innocent's?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-01T03:40:56-08:00","id":1190607,"title":"Hunter's Question Difference between bystander's and Innocent's?","content":"Whats the real difference between an Innocent and a Bystander? Im having a hard time telling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T05:41:35-08:00","id":1190626,"title":"","content":"I tought Innicents were Hunters characterized for having a more open policy towards monsters (many times befriending them) while Bystanders were humans that decided to do nothing or flee when they got faced with the supernatural and thus failed the test to be Imbued (they aren't capital &quot;h&quot; Hunters but rather humans that can see the monsters but can't have Edges, a sort of &quot;ghoul splat&quot; for Hunters, their twilight people)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T14:25:47-08:00","id":1190796,"title":"","content":"This may seem like splitting hairs, but bystanders don't just do nothing, they actively try to shut the heralds out and ignore what's revealed to them. Innocents would instead watch and take in what they see; a very action-oriented schedule might dismiss this as &quot;doing nothing&quot;, but gathering data and doing research still counts. After all, one of the most prominent Judges in the setting is a medical doctor who took very detailed notes on everything that he saw. Innocents are like that, but without the mindset where they have some pre-determined courses of action factored in based on what a monster does; where a Judge is waiting to act and deliver action, the Innocents are adjusting to a new world instead of adjusting their new sights to their old views (and possibly playing the part of infiltrators and spies, but the books flit back and forth on that).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T15:16:44-08:00","id":1190815,"title":"","content":"At the moment of Imbuing, your Creed is based on your reaction. As noted a Bystander balks at the call to do something. It's not just that they don't take some specific action, but they actively choose to not respond. An Innocent responds in a fashion that's based around empathy and understanding. The Imbued have to respond with the resolve to act, but not necessarily do a specific thing in that moment. An Innocent might try to calm a raging monster and soothe them as a direct action, or might try to understand the monster's anger, pain, and frustration so they can better prevent it from happening again.<br /> <br /> As I like to put it, the Mercy Creeds focus on individual monsters rather than thinking about monsters in categories (either the big picture thinking of Vision Creeds, or the dangerous/not-dangerous mentality of Zeal Creeds). Redeemers see a monster for who they could be. Martyrs see a monster for risk they represent. Innocents see monsters for who they are (very importantly not just 'what' they are). On Imbuing a Redeemer needs to do something to try to push the monster to be better, the Martyr needs to risk and sacrifice in proportion to the risk the monster is being, and the Innocent needs to accept that the monster is what it is and to address it on those terms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T13:04:45-08:00","id":1191093,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">Innocents are about Innocence (as in, &quot;until proven guilty&quot;). When confronted with something wrong, the Innocent </span></span><span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#333333\">watches and learns so that he can understand just what it is that is wrong. Monsters are an unknown, and they need to be studied before any action -- be it forgiveness or punishment -- can be taken. Innocents are Mercy oriented toward Vision.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#333333\">Bystanders are about Avoidance. When confronted with something wrong, the Bystander tries to avoid having to deal with it, by ignoring it or running away from it. Monsters should not be, and they need to be avoided at all cost. Bystanders lack Virtue orientation, but if later forced into the Hunt, their potential lack of fixation on Zeal, Mercy and/or Vision may actually end up offering a useful perspective that the Imbued may otherwise miss. </span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}